1: Divide $H$ into sequences of sentences $S = \mathcal{ST}(H) = [s_1, s_2, \dots, s_n]$ ;   
2: Assign $P = [p_{s_1}, p_{s_2}, \dots, p_{s_n}]$ where $p_{s_i}$ is the beginning position of $s_i$ , $i \leq n$ , $i \in \mathbb{Z}^+$ ;   
3: Random select a sentence boundary position $p_{s_k}$ where $k \leq \lceil \frac{n}{2} \rceil, k \in \mathbb{Z}^+$ ;   
4: while $k + l_{\min} \leq n$ do   
5: Random select span length $l \in \mathbb{Z}^{+}, l \in [l_{\min}, min(n - k, l_{\max})]$ ;   
6: Sample continuous sentence spans $S_{\mathrm{span}} = [s_k, s_{k+1}, \dots, s_{k+l}]$ ;   
7: Replace $S_{\mathrm{span}}$ with $S_{\mathrm{span}}' = \mathcal{M}(S_{\mathrm{span}}, \mathrm{context} = S \setminus S_{\mathrm{span}})$ ;   
8: Update $S$ and $P$ ;   
9: Update $n, k$ if sentence number changes;   
10: Assign $k_{\mathrm{end}} = k + \text{len}(S_{\mathrm{span}}')$   
11: Random select $k \in [k_{\mathrm{end}}, \left\lceil \frac{n + k_{\mathrm{end}}}{2} \right\rceil]$ ;   
12: end while   
13: return $C = \text{joint}(S)$ ;

